{"name":"Dazzle and Delight","hex":"#d99b7b","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"dazzle","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To confuse or overpower the sight of (someone or something, such as a sensor) by means of excessive brightness.","To render incapable of thinking clearly; to overwhelm with showiness or brilliance."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A light of dazzling brilliancy.","Showy brilliance that may stop a person from thinking clearly."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dazzle"},{"term":"and","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Symbol","definitions":["ISO 639-3 language code for Ansus."]},{"part":"Conjunction","definitions":["As a coordinating conjunction; expressing two elements to be taken together or in addition to each other.\nUsed simply to connect two noun phrases, adjectives or adverbs. .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}\n\nSimply connecting two clauses or sentences. \n\nIntroducing a clause or sentence which follows on in time or consequence from the first.","Used simply to connect two noun phrases, adjectives or adverbs. .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/and"},{"term":"delight","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Joy; pleasure.","Something that gives great joy or pleasure."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To give delight to; to affect with great pleasure; to please highly.","To have or take great pleasure."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/delight"}],"entries":[],"images":[],"sounds":{"dazzle":[{"type":"audio/wav","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/6/64/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Vealhurl-dazzle.wav?utm_source=en.wiktionary.org&utm_campaign=rest&utm_content=original"},{"type":"audio/mpeg","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/6/64/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Vealhurl-dazzle.wav/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Vealhurl-dazzle.wav.mp3"},{"type":"audio/ogg; codecs=\"vorbis\"","src":"https://uploa